6:1–8:1a The ministry of Stephen is described in four scenes: (1) the appointment of the seven deacons (6:1–7); (2) Stephen’s powerful witness and resulting arrest (6:8–12); (3) Stephen’s trial before the council (6:13–7:56); and (4) Stephen’s execution by stoning (7:57–8:1a). This is an important story since Stephen’s thought lays the groundwork for the rest of the plot of Acts, which will celebrate the geographical and cultural expansion of Christian faith.');

8:1a This darkest of moments harbors hope as we are introduced to the man who will become the greatest of Christian missionaries—the Apostle Paul (see 7:58).
