Paul is anxious to establish important principles in exercising the gift: (1) Public worship should be intelligible. Spiritual gifts used there should edify and encourage (14:1–12); (2) If used publicly, tongues require interpretation and the number of participants should be limited (vv. 5, 13, 27–28; 12:10, 30). To do otherwise detracts from a successful mission (14:16–17, 20–25); (3) Those who use the gift should practice self-control (vv. 13–19, 28); and (4) The use of the gift of tongues should not distract from the more important gift of prophecy (vv. 1, 5; 12:28–31).');
